Install Go (required for xk6 build)

If you don’t have Go:

sudo apt install golang -y

You can verify:

go version

If Go isn't installed correctly, I’ll guide you—but usually this works.

2️⃣ Install xk6 CLI

Run:

go install go.k6.io/xk6/cmd/xk6@latest

This installs xk6 into:

~/go/bin/xk6
3️⃣ Add xk6 to PATH

Run:

export PATH=$PATH:~/go/bin

To make it permanent:

echo 'export PATH=$PATH:~/go/bin' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc
4️⃣ Check if it's working
xk6 --version

You should now see something like:

xk6 v0.x.x
🧱 5️⃣ Build k6 with Redis extension

Now run:

xk6 build --with github.com/grafana/xk6-redis

This produces:

./k6

Then run your dashboard test:

K6_WEB_DASHBOARD=true K6_WEB_DASHBOARD_HOST=0.0.0.0 ./k6 run script.js